# python build artifacts
build/
*.egg-info/

# Gallery kits: build output, not source.
#
# `web/tools/build_figure_kits.py` regenerates every one of these from the
# generators and the gallery page, so git gains nothing by carrying them —
# and a zip is the worst thing to version: already compressed, so git cannot
# delta it, and a rebuild whose content is unchanged can still produce
# different bytes (verified: bar and upset come out byte-identical, horizon
# and voronoi do not).
#
# They are published by uploading web/ to the host by hand, the same way the
# rest of the site is. Rebuild before uploading:
#     python3 web/tools/build_figure_kits.py
# ``*.zip`` alone misses web/kits/fr/, where the French kits land — three
# of them were staged for commit before this was noticed.
web/kits/**/*.zip

# The films: render output, not source.
#
# Same reasoning as the gallery kits above, applied to the whole of web/video/
# and brag-output/out/. An H.264 file is already compressed, so git cannot
# delta it, and a re-render of an unchanged composition does not come out
# byte-identical. The posters are frames pulled straight out of those files, so
# they are the same output wearing a different extension, and the WebVTT tracks
# fall out of a generator that is itself tracked. None of it belongs in a clone.
#
# What stays tracked rebuilds the films from a clone AS FAR AS IT GOES, which is
# not all the way: `python3 brag-output/restore_assets.py` audits the gap and
# names it. Eleven files in brag-output/_assets/ exist nowhere else — a licensed
# music track the whole BEATS grid is measured off, three sound effects, a GSAP
# build whose version is unrecorded, three captures of another project's GUI,
# and its logo. They live in an off-repo archive (~/sauvegardes-sprezzature/),
# restored with `restore_assets.py --fix --seed`. Everything else the repo
# rebuilds itself: the 17 narration WAVs and the five colour-vision frames come
# back byte-for-byte, and the cli-gui form is re-rendered from figure_cli.py,
# the argparse of the shoot, rebuilt from the captures and guarded by
# tests/test_figure_cli.py.
#
#     python3 brag-output/restore_assets.py --fix   # rebuild _assets/ first
#     python3 brag-output/build_films.py            # the 15 compositions
#     cd brag-output/films/<film>-<format>
#     npx hyperframes check                         # the gate before render
#     npx hyperframes render --quality looks --low-memory-mode \
#       --output ../../out/<film>-<format>.mp4
#     ffmpeg -ss <t> -i out/<f>.mp4 -frames:v 1 -q:v 2 out/<f>.jpg
#     python3 brag-output/make_captions.py          # the WebVTT tracks
#     cp brag-output/out/<film>-landscape.{mp4,jpg} web/video/<film>.{mp4,jpg}
# The poster timestamps and every other decision are recorded in
# brag-output/brag-plan.md.
#
# They reach sprezzature.ai the way the kits do, by uploading web/ to the host.
# sftp/UPLOAD-films.txt lists exactly which files that takes.
web/video/
brag-output/out/

# Assets copied into the film projects (fonts, figures, music, narration) and
# the fifteen generated HyperFrames projects. build_films.py rewrites both.
brag-output/_assets/
brag-output/films/
